# D-105 native, the result route (steps/d105-native.md §5): a type reaching a
# result along an edge is admitted as a return value is -- by every field of the result's type:
# `id (Model: m) Model` returns its formal, and `Lacks` (no field `a`) reaches it -- refused at id's
# `return:`.  Before: translated, and the caller read a slot Lacks has not.
Model:
    size_t: a 1U
    size_t: b 2U
end: Model
Lacks:
    size_t: b 20U
end: Lacks
fn: rd (Model: m) size_t
return: m\a
fn: id (Model: m) Model
return: m
fn: go () size_t
    o: merge Lacks
    return: rd(id(o))
size_t: got 0U
got: go()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
